Subject: [PATCH] Copy each decoded chunk out of the decoder's memory

XzReadableStream enqueued a view into the wasm output buffer, then
reset the buffer for the next chunk. A consumer that has not copied
the view by the time the next pull runs reads the next chunk's bytes
in its place: the output has the right length and wrong contents.
Whether that happens depends on the stream scheduling of the engine
(node: every time; Chrome: rarely), which is how a NAR decoded fine
on one browser and failed to parse on another. Enqueue a copy.

---
--- a/xzwasm.js
+++ b/xzwasm.js
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@
         if (result !== XZ_OK && result !== XZ_STREAM_END) {
             throw new Error(`get_next_output failed with error code ${result}`);
         }
-        const outChunk = this.mem8.subarray(this.outStart, this.outStart + /* outPos */ this.mem32[5]);
+        const outChunk = this.mem8.slice(this.outStart, this.outStart + this.mem32[5]);
         return { outChunk, finished: result === XZ_STREAM_END };
     }
 
